#!/bin/bash

set -eu
set -o pipefail

VERSION="${1}"
ISOS="${2}"
RELEASE_BRANCH="${3}"
MATCHING_JENKINS_IMAGES_BUILD_ID="${4}"

./bin/automailer.py <<EOF
To: rm@tails.net, sajolida@pimienta.org
Subject: Testing Tails ${VERSION:?}
X-Attach: $(/bin/ls -1 "$ISOS/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}".{build-manifest,packages} "$ISOS/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}".{iso,img}.sig | tr '\n' ,)

You can now start testing Tails ${VERSION}:

1. Download the images
======================

Either use \`git-annex\` or download from
https://nightly.tails.net/build_Tails_ISO_${RELEASE_BRANCH:?}/builds/${MATCHING_JENKINS_IMAGES_BUILD_ID:?}/archive/build-artifacts/

2. Verify the images
====================

Verify the downloaded images *using the signatures attached to this email*.

To verify the images, run:

    gpg --verify /path/to/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}.img.sig tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}.img
    gpg --verify /path/to/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}.iso.sig tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}.iso

3. Save the attached build-manifest
===================================

Replace any build-manifest you've downloaded with the one *attached to this email*.

If you've downloaded the images with \`git-annex\`, you can inject
the attachment into your local annex, to keep everything in one single place:

    git annex reinject --known /path/to/tails-amd64-${VERSION:?}.build-manifest

4. Start testing :)
===================
EOF
